From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] print status: the AD5X's print start steps as Kiln runs them

The step list on the print status screen read the AD5X's start with the
generic profile and got it wrong in several ways. The first heat warms
bed and nozzle together, but the heater signals made a "Heating nozzle"
row that flipped back to the bed within a second (always 0s), and a
nozzle that was still hot made none, so the rows changed from print to
print. The box purge counted as the purge step. The upcoming rows came
in the order the macro scan saw the commands (Kiln's PRINT_START clears
the mesh before it homes and purges at the box before the edge clean),
so Purge came before Cleaning. Patch 0062's status line above the list
could disagree with the row below it ("Checking Z" over a current "Heat
soak"), and a step past its prediction counted down to a stuck "0s".

The AD5X now has its own print start profile (ad5x.json). Kiln's
PRINT_START names every step, as an M117 and an "echo:" console line,
and the profile reads only those texts: Homing; "Heating bed and
nozzle" and "Purging at the box" are one Heating step (the box purge
and the brushing run while the soak's clock already runs); "Heat soak
m:ss"; "Checking Z" and "Cleaning nozzle on the bed edge" are the
Cleaning step; "Bed mesh: ..."; "Heating to print temperature" is
Heating nozzle; "Prime line" or "Loading first colour" is Purge. With
"narrated_steps" the collector takes no phase from the heaters, from
extrusion or from probe lines outside the mesh. "// Bed heat soak:
N s" is not a step: it is printed when the bed arrives, while the
nozzle still heats.

Its "checklist" block lists the steps in the order the AD5X runs them:
Homing, Heating, Heat soak, Cleaning, Bed mesh, Heating nozzle, Purge.
The macro scan only drops a step it can see and did not find. A step
the start went past without running (no soak on a hot bed, no mesh
with the centre Z check) leaves the list. The running step's row shows
the printer's own words ("Heat soak 0:09", "Checking Z", "Cleaning
nozzle on the bed edge"), done rows their step name; 0062's separate
line is gone. A running step past its prediction shows no time instead
of 0s, and a step whose words carry the printer's own countdown ("Heat
soak 1:41") shows no guess from past prints beside it. Other printers' profiles have none of this and keep upstream's
list.

Tests: the AD5X texts, with and without the "echo: " prefix, and the
lines around them that name no step; the AD5X's profile in the printer
database; its messages and labels in every catalog; the step order
against Kiln's macros as the scan reads them, a macro without a mesh or
a clean, and no scan; whole starts replayed (box purge, soak, mesh,
first colour; no box purge, no soak, centre Z check, prime line; a hot
nozzle with a cold bed), with the heaters as they move; the M117 alone;
the printer's words leaving with their step; the default profile's
checklist unchanged; the rows the screen draws.
